preConditionHook:
// 'The first bear spike in a strong bull trend is almost always just a bull
// flag.' The FIRST against-trend trend bar in a long while printed within the
// last flagBars bars, nothing like it appeared in the strongBars bars BEFORE
// it, and this bar has now closed above its high -- buy. Short is the mirror.
//
// KEPT WHOLE rather than split, and the reason is structural: the 'no other
// opposite trend bar in the preceding strongBars bars' term is
// StrongTrendBarCount negated, but it must be measured FROM THE FOUND BAR k,
// not from bar 0, and a pane cannot express a window whose origin is data.
// The same goes for the trigger, close[0] > high[k], a comparison at a
// VARIABLE lag. Everything is bounded -- at most flagBars for the scan and
// strongBars for the clean run -- so the deepest bar touched is
// flagBars + strongBars.
//
// 'FIRST' is the smallest offset, carried by the kBear == -1 guard rather
// than a loop break, because EasyLanguage has none and both twins must run
// the same iterations.
//
// THE -1 GUARD IS LOAD-BEARING TWICE. EasyLanguage does not short-circuit, so
// 'kBear != -1 && close[0] > high[kBear]' would still evaluate high[-1], a
// future bar, in the twin. Both the clean-run scan and the trigger therefore
// sit inside an IF on the guard rather than behind an AND, in both twins.
//
// A trend bar is StrongTrendBarRun's definition: it closes in its own
// direction and its body is at least bodyFraction of the bar's own range,
// written as a product because EL raises a runtime divide-by-zero on a
// zero-range bar and that is legal data. Brooks states the setup only for the
// FIRST opposite spike, which is why the zero-count window is part of the
// rule and not a separate filter.
//
// The flags are class members and persist across bars, so each is set at the
// top of its block rather than relied on to start clear.
kBear = -1;
kBull = -1;
for (int k = 1; k <= (int)flagBars; ++k) {
    if (kBear == -1 && el_lt(close[k], open[k])
        && el_ge(open[k] - close[k], bodyFraction * (high[k] - low[k]))) {
        kBear = k;
    }
    if (kBull == -1 && el_gt(close[k], open[k])
        && el_ge(close[k] - open[k], bodyFraction * (high[k] - low[k]))) {
        kBull = k;
    }
}
cleanBear = true;
if (kBear != -1) {
    for (int j = kBear + 1; j <= kBear + (int)strongBars; ++j) {
        if (el_lt(close[j], open[j])
            && el_ge(open[j] - close[j], bodyFraction * (high[j] - low[j]))) {
            cleanBear = false;
        }
    }
}
cleanBull = true;
if (kBull != -1) {
    for (int j = kBull + 1; j <= kBull + (int)strongBars; ++j) {
        if (el_gt(close[j], open[j])
            && el_ge(close[j] - open[j], bodyFraction * (high[j] - low[j]))) {
            cleanBull = false;
        }
    }
}
longSig = false;
if (kBear != -1) {
    longSig = cleanBear && el_gt(close[0], high[kBear]);
}
shortSig = false;
if (kBull != -1) {
    shortSig = cleanBull && el_lt(close[0], low[kBull]);
}
